<http://opendata.inra.fr/AHOL/AHOL_0005001> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/upper_level_interpretation> "The definition reads like three different definitions copy pasted. \"Damage on health\" is very broad and encompasses entities like suffocation which is clearly not a disease. \"The modifications of an organism defending itself against an infection or other damager (!) factor\" does exclude a lot of entities typically denoted as diseases. There could be a potential malignancy against which is no observable sign of defence. \"Perturbation of the animal's normal function\" is again very broad. Holding my breath can be argued as a perturbation of normal function. disease is_a animal health trait is_a animal health trait ontology for livestock seems like non-adherence to class hierarchy modelling principles." .
<http://pgxo.loria.fr/Disease> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Monnin P; Legrand J; Husson G; Ringot P; Tchechmedjiev A; Jonquet C; Napoli A; Coulet A (2019) PGxO and PGxLOD: a reconciliation of pharmacogenomic knowledge of various provenances, enabling further comparison. BMC Bioinformatics. doi:10.1186/s12859-019-2693-9" .
