<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HINO_0015722> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/upper_level_interpretation> "is_a ino:human molecular pathway is_a ino:pathway is_a ino:interaction_network is a bfo:process. Thus, disease is a process with probably proteins as participant. Hence, ogms:disease and ino:disease are not equivalent although both are OBO ontologies. In this very narrow scope of disease as a pathway the definition seems sound but leaves the clinical view of disease totally untouched and unreusable for this use case." .
