<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MPATH_0> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/upper_level_interpretation> "mpath:pathological entity is_a mpath:pathological phenotype observation. Grandchild is for example neoplasm is_a pathological anatomical entity is_a pathological entity. Thus, MAPTH seems not like an ontology in a sense of modelling our shared conceptualisation of reality but rather an endeavour to group certain observations into buckets. Because clearly, a neoplasm isn't an observation but the observation entity is created when observing a neoplasm. There is no definition of pathological." .
