<http://www.case.edu/EpilepsyOntology.owl#Disease> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/upper_level_interpretation> "No comment, no definition, but the superclass as BFO class is expressive enough to convey some meaning. The publication doesn't mention the modelling choice different from OGMS (https://doi.org/10.1136/amiajnl-2013-001696). Strangely, not bfo:disposition nor bfo:realizable entity are reused in EPSO. Entities like epso:Insomnia and epso:Brain neoplasm are both leaves of epso:Disorder." .
