<http://www.limics.fr/ontologies/ontolurgences#EtatPathologique> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/provenance_quality> "good" .
<http://www.limics.fr/ontologies/ontolurgences#EtatPathologique> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/review_date> "2026-07-09" .
<http://www.limics.fr/ontologies/ontolurgences#EtatPathologique> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/review_notes> "Manual replacement target for ONTOLURGENCES syndrome; review EtatPathologique instead of Syndrome." .
<http://www.limics.fr/ontologies/ontolurgences#EtatPathologique> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/reviewer> "MM" .
<http://www.limics.fr/ontologies/ontolurgences#EtatPathologique> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/upper_level_interpretation> "No definition, no comment. Grounded on Menelas top ontology with etat pathologique is_a etat interne is_an objet intentionel is_an objet abstrait. The definition of objet intentionnel explicitly says it is an object \"qui ne peut être trouvé dans le monde physique, ni dans le monde abstrait ou temporel.\" So the class is defined as not belonging to the abstract world and is then subsumed under objet abstrait. That's a genus/differentia failure. And a disease in common sense definetely belongs to the \"monde physique\". So another contradiction here." .
