<http://www.semanticweb.org/ontologies/chronic-diease-patient-education-ontology#Disease> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/upper_level_interpretation> "No comment, definition or superclass. No paper. The ontology description says: \"The constructed ontology mainly consists of two levels. Level 1 includes 5 terms: demographic, disease, vital sign, lifestyle and medication, which describe the characteristics contained in the patient data, as well as the topics of education materials. Leve 2 contains the detailed elements for each Level 1 class.\"" .
