<http://www.semanticweb.org/ontologies/epo.owl#HealthCondition> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/upper_level_interpretation> "Clear Menelas top-grounding. The class does not read as a disease entity itself, but as a clinical/phenotypic manifestation or diagnostic interpretation of an underlying internal state. However, internal state is modeled as a sibling rather than a superclass or defining substrate, and both health condition and internal state are placed under maternal state. This makes the modelling highly scope-bound to early pregnancy/maternal context, with no clear built-in reusability as a general disease or health-condition class." .
