<urn:agi-folder:disease> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/review_notes> "although denoted as taxonomy, the hierarchy contains false or at least strange is_a relationships.  1. bpt:Wilson's Disease is_a bpt:Wilson's disease.   2. bpt:Oxidative Stress in vitiligo is_a bpt:Vitiligo" .
<urn:agi-folder:disease> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/reviewer> "MM" .
<urn:agi-folder:disease> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/term> "disease" .
<urn:agi-folder:disease> <https://example.org/disease-review/ap/upper_level_interpretation> "bpt:Disease as a subclass of bpt:Pathway focusses on molecular interactions rather than clinical presentation. All bpt:Pathway leafs are proper process-like pathways. But, the classes in between are typically perceived as continuants. Full example: bpt:CCR5 Signaling in Macrophages is_a bpt:blood is_a bpt:Tissues is_a bpt: Anatomy index is_an Index is_a Pathways." .
